center("Studio G, Strand, Cape Town · 2026", 22, 160, false, true);
center("G", 28, 200, true);
center("Draft v0.1 — production draft for the author’s ruling. Number, title, and lock status are open.", 18, 240, false, true);

// ============================== ARTIST'S NOTE ==============================
h1("Artist’s Note");
body("*What this paper does — and why.*");
body("This paper names and prices the cost the corpus has already admitted to. AP06 priced the flow: the leakage, one unpaired ε shed at every instant, bounded by C, the constant of every leakage denominator. AP28 named a second cost without pricing it — “Gravity is the cost the arena pays to keep the break open” — and then derived G as though the arena paid nothing to constitute the configurations it holds. This paper prices the constitution. The price is the coupling configuration cost — the snap cost, CCC — and it is the axiom’s own arithmetic: one unpaired element, held once, per configuration. The realised gravitational coupling is the structural coupling divided by (1 + ε).");
body("The argument in one breath. Every Actualization State instant produces exactly one unpaired ε (AP43 D5, carried by AP06 §6). At every instant after a configuration exists, that instant’s ε is shed at the boundary: the leakage. At the constitution instant itself the ε cannot be shed — if it were, nothing present at that instant would hold the first record open, and by Axiom R the crack would heal and the configuration would not persist. Therefore it is held. Held once, forever: the commitment. Its size is not a choice. Axiom R does not permit selective persistence — a configuration snaps entire or not at all — so constitution is a single event, and a single event carries a single ε. Per configuration, not per channel. One ε, once.");
body("What it touches and what it cannot touch. Because the commitment is per configuration, it dresses every bound mass by the same factor and cancels identically in every mass ratio. The proton result of AP30 — inside experimental uncertainty — is preserved to the digit, and AP30 §7’s reading of its own residual stands unamended. The commitment survives only where a mass stands outside a ratio, and in the corpus that is one place: G. The realised prediction is G = α_em²¹ × (1 + 1/π) / (1 + α_em) × ℏc/m_e² = 6.6719 × 10⁻¹¹ N·m²/kg² — closing about ninety-five per cent of AP28’s 0.69% and moving the prediction from outside every laboratory determination ever made to the low edge of the measured landscape.");
body("The honesty box. The load-bearing proposition — held, not shed, at constitution — is derived here at the structural register, with its record-algebra formalisation named as a debt, not hidden. The residual that remains after the commitment, about −0.036%, flips sign: it can no longer be absorbed by downward apparatus leakage, and it is reported open and unattributed. Six kill switches engage, and the first of them is aimed at the author: KS-CCC.1 fires if any commitment magnitude is ever published whose selection depended on comparison with measurement. Two clean fractions the data volunteered after the fact — 20/21 of ε, 17/18 of ε — are named in §10 for exactly one purpose: to be fenced. Seen, and refused.");
body("The completeness claim. This paper adds no new axiom, no new measured input, and no new number. It reads a sentence the corpus locked years ago and prices it with the element the axiom already provides. The description was incomplete by one commitment. Now it is written down.");
center("✨", 24, 120);
center("the420code.org", 20, 40, false, true);
center("Copyleft 2026", 20, 240, false, true);

// ============================== ORIENTATION ==============================
h1("Orientation");
h2("Where this paper fits");
body("This paper sits in Notebook IV (Forces and Constants), immediately after AP28 (The Constant), whose result it completes and — on adoption — amends. It depends on Notebook I for the axiom 1:1 + 1×ε @ AS and the four conditions {S, B, R, C}; on AP06 for the leakage structure and Identification 6.1 (ε ≡ η; ε = α_em at the coupling boundary); on AP28 for the coupling graph, the per-channel coupling, the R-reading of G, and the no-selective-persistence clause; on AP24 for the licence of multiple independent readings of one ε; on AP10 for the three dimensions and the identification of the 1:1 as the substrate; on AP43 D5 for the one-ε-per-instant account; on AP29 for mass as coupling capacity actualised; and on AP20 for the unconditional floor.");
body("Downstream, on adoption only: the wording of KS-R.7; AP28 §6–§7; Ø Predictions Part II, where this paper enters as a third candidate for the 0.69% and reinterprets the Appendix C proposal as a discriminator; the G passages of the Proofs and Prose registers; and every user of the holding limit κ, which moves with the realised coupling and whose dependents are to be audited before adoption (D-CCC.3).");
h2("Reading order within this paper");
body("Front to back. Sections 2 through 5 are the spine: the constitution record, the held commitment, the per-configuration count, and the form of the correction. Section 3 carries the load. Sections 6 and 7 place the commitment and defend the double entry. Section 8 is architecture — the ten vertices — and nothing numerical rests on it. Sections 9 through 11 are empirical: the prediction, the discipline that fences it, and its standing among the candidates Ø Predictions holds open. If you are reading for the result only, §5 and §9. If you are reading for rigour, §3. If you are reading to check that the author has not fooled himself, §10.");
h2("How to read this paper");
body("Two registers alternate as the material requires, as everywhere in Notebook IV. Formal blocks open with a bold label (Proposition, Corollary, Kill Switch) and close with the mark ∎. The connective passages speak directly. One register discipline specific to this paper: the number appears once, in §9, after the structure is complete, and §10 exists to keep it that way.");
h2("A note on notation");
body("α_G is AP28’s structural gravitational coupling, α_em²¹ × (1 + 1/π). α_G* is the realised coupling, α_G / (1 + ε), introduced here. κ is the holding limit; κ* = α_G* ℏc / 2 is its realised value. ε carries one structural meaning throughout the corpus — the unique unpaired element of Axiom B — and one value at the coupling boundary, ε = α_em ≈ 1/137, inherited from Identification 6.1 (AP06). This paper adds no identification of its own. “Snap” means the constitution event: the single Actualization State instant at which a configuration’s first record is written and holds. “Provisioned” and “realised” name the two totals the axiom itself distinguishes: 1:1 + 1×ε, and the 1:1 that persists. CCC is the once-held commitment; TLC is the per-instant leakage of AP06. “Vertex” and “edge” refer to the coupling graph AP28 Propositions 1–2 prove: ten vertices, twenty-one edges.");

// ============================== CONTENTS ==============================
h1("Contents");
body("**0 — Dependency and Scope**  ·  what this paper does · dependencies · axiom mapping · epistemic status · kill switch summary · debts · items held open · relationships");
body("**1 — Definitions**  ·  the snap · provisioned and realised · the two costs — commitment and leakage");
body("**2 — The Constitution Record**  ·  Proposition 1: every persisting configuration has a unique first record");
